							"text": "Here are the facts for the card:\n\n*   WebAssembly (Wasm) is a low-level, assembly-like binary instruction format.\n*   It's a compilation target for languages like C, C++, Rust, and C#.\n*   Its main goal is to enable high-performance code to run on the web at near-native speed.\n*   It runs alongside and complements JavaScript, allowing interoperation.\n*   WebAssembly executes in a memory-safe, sandboxed environment, enforcing browser security policies.\n*   It is portable and can be used in non-web environments too, via WebAssembly System Interface (WASI).\n*   It's designed to be debuggable with a human-readable text format.\n*   It was developed by engineers from Google, Mozilla, Microsoft, and Apple, and is a W3C standard."
						}
					],
